(1) There shall be for the Commission a Governing Council (in this Act referred to as"the Council") which shall be responsible for the discharge of the functions of the Commission.
(2) The Council shall consist of-
(a) a chairman who shall be a retired Justice of the Supreme Court of Nigeria orthe Court of Appeal or a retired judge of the High Court of a State;
(b) a representative each of the following Federal Ministries-
(i) Justice;
(ii) Foreign Affairs;
(iii) Internal Affairs;
(c) three representatives ofregistered human rights organisations in Nigeria;
(d) two legal practitioners who shall not have less than ten years post qualificationexperience;
(e) three representatives of the media, at least, two of whom shall be from the private sector;
(f) three other persons to represent a variety of interests; and
(g) the executive secretary of the Commission.
(3) The chairman and members of the Commission shall be-
(a) persons of proven integrity; and
(b) appointed by the President, on the recommendation of the Attorney-General ofthe Federation.
(4) The supplementary provisions set out in the Schedule to this Act shall have effectwith respect to the proceedings of the Council and the other matters contained therein.[Schedule.]

